  "question": {
    "text": "A metal $M$ on heating in nitrogen gas gives $Y$. $Y$ on treatment with $\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}$ gives a colourless gas which when passed through $\\mathrm{CuSO}_4$ solution gives a blue colour. $Y$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "zceNx",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{NH}_3$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "7FEvM",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{Mg}\\left(\\mathrm{NO}_3\\right)_2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bdDf9",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{Mg}_3 \\mathrm{~N}_2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "cSmih",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{MgO}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\underset{M}{3 \\mathrm{Mg}}+\\mathrm{N}_2 \\longrightarrow \\underset{Y}{\\mathrm{Mg}_3} \\mathrm{~N}_2$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\underset{Y}{\\mathrm{Mg}_3 \\mathrm{~N}_2}+6 \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O} \\longrightarrow 3 \\mathrm{Mg}(\\mathrm{OH})_2+\\underset{\\text { colourless }}{2 \\mathrm{NH}_3 \\uparrow} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{CuSO}_4+4 \\mathrm{NH}_3 \\longrightarrow\\left[\\mathrm{Cu}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_4\\right] \\mathrm{SO}_4 \\\\\n&\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBlue complex",
